abyrinth enters the battlefield, you won't be able to draw more cards that turn.","oracle_id":"1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec","published_at":"2014-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you haven't drawn any cards in a turn, and a spell or ability would cause you to draw multiple cards, you'll just draw one card.","oracle_id":"1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec","published_at":"2014-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can draw a maximum of one card on each player's turn. Subsequent card draws are ignored.","oracle_id":"1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec","published_at":"2014-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An ability that triggers when a player casts a spell resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger. It resolves even if that spell is countered.","oracle_id":"82e6da87-f8a4-4897-bf0f-c0f2cd06b8b1","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Players can cast spells and activate abilities after the triggered ability resolves but before the spell that caused it to trigger does.","oracle_id":"82e6da87-f8a4-4897-bf0f-c0f2cd06b8b1","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Sacrificing Seal of Removal is the cost to activate its ability. Once you activate the ability, no player can do anything to Seal of Removal to stop you from activating it. Notably, if you cast Seal of Removal during your turn, you'll have priority to activate its ability before anyone can respond to stop you.","oracle_id":"f0801029-bcf7-4bdb-84bf-e88dcaa9dc03","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
